          "notes": "gbrain's shipped defaults as init resolves them with Voyage, OpenAI and Anthropic keys present: PGLite engine, voyage:voyage-4 at 1024 dimensions, search mode tokenmax (init's auto pick: reranker voyage:rerank-2.5 on, LLM expansion on, search limit 50, contextual retrieval per-chunk synopsis, semantic cache as gbrain's availability gate sets it), internal models from gbrain's tier defaults. These are the expected values; /capabilities adds `resolved`, read from the stack's reference install (gbrain search modes --json, gbrain models --json, config.json) with its sha256, and every later install and every serve start must resolve to the same hash."
        }
      },
      "install": {
        "recipe": [
          "bun install -g github:garrytan/gbrain#<GBRAIN_SHA> (image build)",
          "config.json provider_base_urls.{voyage,openai,anthropic} -> the egress relay to the metering proxy, written before init",
          "gbrain init --pglite --json (dummy VOYAGE_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the environment)",
          "gbrain apply-migrations --yes --non-interactive --no-autopilot-install (the setup step gbrain's postinstall runs; bun install -g blocks postinstall scripts)",
          "the scripted 'defaults' reply: every first_run_decisions default option's argv, as init printed it",
          "gbrain serve --surface starter over MCP stdio (the registration gbrain's harness_wiring option names)"
        ],
        "first_run_defaults": {
          "search_mode": "tokenmax (gbrain config set search.mode tokenmax)",
          "writeback": "salient (gbrain config set memory.auto_writeback salient)",
          "harness_wiring": "skip in init's terms (no argv); the shim is the agent host and registers gbrain serve --surface starter"
        }
      },
      "time": "in-text",
      "time_notes": "Each session is a type: conversation page whose frontmatter carries the session date and whose turns carry the session time in gbrain's conversation-parser anchor shape (**Speaker** (YYYY-MM-DD h:mm AM): text). query takes no as-of date, so query_time is not sent; synthesize takes none either (relative-time questions resolve against the run date, the shipped behavior). think receives the question date as reference_date.",
      "provenance": {
        "status": "exact",
        "mechanism": "One page per session at conversations/<date>/<source id>; every returned row names its page slug, which maps to exactly one ingested source id. Rows from pages gbrain created itself (none under the defaults on conversation pages) report unavailable."
      },
      "delete": "unsupported",
      "delete_notes": "The starter surface has no page delete; delete_page is a full-surface op and the scoreboard calls only starter ops.",
      "readiness": "put_page returns when the write commits (pending receipts are polled with get_write_request until terminal; a failed or conflicting receipt is a product error, and a replay with the same request id returns gbrain's stored receipt); embeddings are a later persistence effect. /finish stops serve, runs gbrain doctor --json with the brain to itself (a doctor under a live serve reports details.reason live_serve and fails the barrier), requires every expected page and 0 chunks missing embeddings, restarts serve while coverage is short (its persistence consumer drains the effects) until timeout_s, then reads gbrain's job queue (gbrain jobs list --json) and the outbox effects still pending (list_write_requests) and keeps serve up for drain rounds while any can still run, up to the same timeout_s, recording what is left as background_liabilities, and confirms every page through list_pages.",
      "namespace": "one brain per namespace: a clean scripted install per namespace at one fixed GBRAIN_HOME, verified against the stack's reference install (resolved configuration, config hash without its install timestamp, starter tools/list). Brains move between /data/ns/<ns> and GBRAIN_HOME by rename and are never copied: gbrain binds a brain's content checkout to its inode and birth time, so a copied brain refuses writes with recovery_required.",
      "parallel_namespaces": false,
      "retrieval_policies": {
        "vendor-default": {
          "settings": {},
          "notes": "Bare query: no limit (tokenmax resolves 50), no token_budget, expansion on by default, auto delivery (whole conversation pages up to 24,000 tokens). token_budget is refused: without return_unit it switches query to chunk delivery (src/core/ops/search.ts:131, src/core/search/evidence-delivery.ts:200)."
        },
        "fixed-evidence": {
          "settings": {
            "limit": 50,
            "autocut": false
          },
          "notes": "query with limit 50 and autocut off, still no token_budget, so delivery stays auto; the harness packs 2k/8k/16k from the delivered pages."
        },
        "allowed_settings_overrides": [
          "limit",
          "autocut",
          "expand",
          "on_degraded (error | report)"
        ],
        "on_degraded": "error",
        "degraded_reads": "Every query response's _meta.retrieval (vector_enabled, expansion_applied, cache, degraded, projection_readiness, vector_pool_underfilled, crag, delivery fallbacks and dropped_reasons) and its gbrain notices are returned under raw. A harness failure is: any degraded stage (the reranker reports failure as reranker_skipped, rerank_passthrough or rerank_failed; expansion as expansion_failed), rows without the confidence block's top_rerank_score in a reranked mode (meta.rerank is System One's field and stays absent under the defaults), expansion_applied false in an expansion mode (gbrain's expansion falls back to the bare query silently, for example on a proxy 402), a disabled vector arm, a projection that is not ready, a delivery fallback that is not shipped behavior (fetch_timeout, fetch_failed, row_limit, unsealed_page, anchor_not_located, page_missing or any unknown reason), or a delivery unit other than auto. With on_degraded error (the default) /retrieve answers HTTP 503 with error kind invalid_request, which memory-qa records as harness_invalid and retries; with on_degraded report it returns the items with raw.classification.outcome harness_invalid. A semantic cache hit, an underfilled vector pool, dropped delivery blocks and the preregistered shipped-behavior delivery fallbacks (redaction_unmapped: gbrain's secret redactor changed a block's text; no_text_chunks: a page with no text chunks delivers its hit as a chunk; the set is GBRAIN_SHIPPED_FALLBACKS and /capabilities shows it under shipped_behavior) are recorded under raw.classification.recorded as delivery_fallback:<reason>, counted in GET /health shipped_fallbacks, never classified as degraded and never answered with the 503.",
        "item_mapping": "One item per query row in gbrain's rank order. Rows are gbrain's lean remote rows (the shape an agent reads); chunk_text is the delivered text (a whole conversation page under auto delivery). A type: conversation row -> type episode (chunk when gbrain marks it truncated), anything else chunk; source_ids is the page's source id, provenance exact."
      },
      "own_answer": {
        "route": "POST /answer {ns, question, query_time, mode: synthesize | think, model}",
        "synthesize": "the starter synthesize verb with gbrain's configured default model; synthesis_status ok -> outcome scored; extractive_fallback -> scored with degraded extractive_fallback (its own column); an unavailable error (dummy-key or compose failure path) -> harness_invalid.",
        "think": "full surface only (GBRAIN_FULL_SURFACE=1 serves --surface full; every other call still uses starter ops, checked against the starter tools/list captured at template build): think with model = the reader and reference_date = the question date."
      },
      "streaming": "disabled",
